CAT = "cpafarStatements"; SEG = "STM"
Q = [
("Before its year-end statements are issued, a company replaces a note due in nine months with a five-year note from the same lender. On the year-end balance sheet the original note is classified as:",
 "A noncurrent liability", ["A current liability", "Current, with note disclosure only", "A deferred credit"],
 "Under ASC 470-10, a short-term obligation is excluded from current liabilities when the entity refinances it on a long-term basis after the balance sheet date but before the statements are issued. Disclosure alone is not enough because the refinancing has actually happened."),
("Which item is reported in other comprehensive income by a for-profit company?",
 "Foreign currency translation adjustment", ["Unrealized gain on equity securities", "Gain on early extinguishment of debt", "Foreign currency transaction loss"],
 "Translation adjustments from converting a foreign subsidiary's statements go to OCI. Changes in the fair value of equity securities with readily determinable fair values and foreign currency transaction gains and losses go through net income."),
("A company reports sales of $900,000, sales returns of $30,000, cost of goods sold of $520,000 and selling expenses of $110,000. Gross profit on a multi-step income statement is:",
 "$350,000", ["$380,000", "$240,000", "$270,000"],
 "Net sales are $900,000 minus $30,000 = $870,000, and gross profit is $870,000 minus $520,000 = $350,000. Selling expenses come after gross profit, and $380,000 forgets the returns."),
("The results of a component that qualifies as a discontinued operation are reported in the income statement:",
 "Net of tax, below continuing operations", ["Pretax, within operating expenses", "Net of tax, in retained earnings", "Pretax, in other comprehensive income"],
 "Discontinued operations are shown net of their tax effect in a separate section after income from continuing operations. They are part of net income, not OCI or a direct equity entry."),
("Net income is $210,000. Depreciation is $45,000, accounts receivable rose $18,000, inventory fell $12,000, accounts payable fell $9,000 and a $6,000 gain was recognized on selling equipment. Cash provided by operating activities is:",
 "$234,000", ["$246,000", "$252,000", "$189,000"],
 "$210,000 + $45,000 - $18,000 + $12,000 - $9,000 - $6,000 = $234,000. The gain is subtracted because the cash proceeds belong in investing activities; adding it gives $246,000."),
("A for-profit company reporting under U.S. GAAP pays interest on its bank loan. The cash paid is classified in the statement of cash flows as:",
 "Operating activities", ["Financing activities", "Investing activities", "A noncash disclosure only"],
 "U.S. GAAP classifies interest paid as an operating outflow because interest expense enters net income. Repaying the loan principal is a financing outflow."),
("Cash received from selling a used delivery truck is reported in the statement of cash flows as:",
 "An investing inflow", ["An operating inflow", "A financing inflow", "A noncash adjustment"],
 "Proceeds from disposing of property, plant and equipment are investing inflows. Any gain on the sale is removed from net income in the operating section under the indirect method."),
("A company acquires a building by signing a $1,500,000 mortgage note with the seller, with no cash changing hands. In the statement of cash flows the transaction is:",
 "Disclosed as a noncash activity", ["An investing outflow and financing inflow", "An operating outflow", "Not reported in any form"],
 "Significant investing and financing activities that involve no cash are excluded from the body of the statement and disclosed separately, in a schedule or the notes."),
("Beginning retained earnings were $400,000. A prior-period error correction increases them by $25,000 net of tax. Net income is $150,000 and cash dividends declared are $60,000. Ending retained earnings are:",
 "$515,000", ["$490,000", "$575,000", "$465,000"],
 "$400,000 + $25,000 = $425,000 restated beginning balance, plus $150,000 net income minus $60,000 dividends gives $515,000. Ignoring the correction gives $490,000."),
("A parent acquired 80% of a subsidiary, and the noncontrolling interest was measured at $160,000, with no fair value adjustments left to amortize. This year the subsidiary earns $90,000 and pays $30,000 in dividends. The noncontrolling interest at year-end is:",
 "$172,000", ["$178,000", "$160,000", "$220,000"],
 "The noncontrolling interest takes its 20% share of the subsidiary's income and dividends: $160,000 + $18,000 - $6,000 = $172,000. Leaving out its share of the dividends gives $178,000."),
("In a consolidated balance sheet, the noncontrolling interest in a subsidiary is reported:",
 "In equity, apart from the parent's", ["Between liabilities and equity", "As a long-term liability", "Only in the notes to the statements"],
 "ASC 810 requires the noncontrolling interest to be presented within equity, separately from the parent's equity. The old mezzanine presentation is not used for ordinary noncontrolling interests."),
("A parent sold inventory costing $40,000 to its subsidiary for $50,000. At year-end the subsidiary still holds 30% of the goods. The unrealized intercompany profit eliminated is:",
 "$3,000", ["$10,000", "$7,000", "$15,000"],
 "The profit on the sale is $10,000, and only the 30% still in the group's inventory is unrealized: $10,000 x 30% = $3,000. The $7,000 on goods resold to outsiders has been realized."),
("A 75%-owned subsidiary owes its parent $45,000 on an intercompany loan at year-end. In the consolidated balance sheet this balance is:",
 "Eliminated in full", ["Eliminated to the parent's share", "Shown as a related-party asset", "Reclassified to equity"],
 "Consolidated statements present the group as one entity, so all intercompany receivables and payables are eliminated in full, whatever the ownership percentage."),
("A parent owns 70% of a subsidiary. The parent's own income, excluding income from the subsidiary, is $500,000 and the subsidiary's net income is $200,000. Consolidated net income attributable to the parent is:",
 "$640,000", ["$700,000", "$560,000", "$500,000"],
 "Consolidated net income is $700,000, of which $60,000 (30% of $200,000) is attributable to the noncontrolling interest. The parent's share is $500,000 + $140,000 = $640,000."),
("A U.S. company buys inventory for 100,000 euros on November 1, when the euro is worth $1.10, and pays on January 15. On December 31 the euro is worth $1.14. At year-end the company records:",
 "A $4,000 loss in net income", ["A $4,000 gain in net income", "A $4,000 loss in OCI", "No entry until it pays"],
 "The euro payable is remeasured at the year-end rate: 100,000 x ($1.14 - $1.10) = $4,000 more owed. A foreign currency transaction loss goes through net income, not OCI."),
("A U.S. company holds a receivable of 300,000 Canadian dollars recorded at $0.74. At year-end the Canadian dollar is worth $0.71. The company recognizes:",
 "A $9,000 loss", ["A $9,000 gain", "A $6,000 loss", "No adjustment"],
 "The receivable will now bring in fewer U.S. dollars: 300,000 x ($0.74 - $0.71) = $9,000 transaction loss in net income. A falling foreign currency hurts a holder of a foreign currency receivable."),
("Which item belongs in the summary of significant accounting policies?",
 "The inventory costing method", ["The composition of inventory", "Maturities of long-term debt", "Amount of rent paid"],
 "The policies note describes the methods chosen, such as FIFO or LIFO and depreciation methods. Balances and their composition are disclosed in other notes, not in the policies summary."),
("For long-term borrowings, a company must disclose the combined maturities:",
 "For each of the next five years", ["For each of the next ten years", "For the next year only", "Only if debt covenants exist"],
 "ASC 470-10 requires the combined aggregate amount of maturities and sinking fund requirements for each of the five years following the balance sheet date."),
("A winery ages its wine for three years before sale, and its normal operating cycle is about three years. On a classified balance sheet the aging wine is:",
 "Current, within the operating cycle", ["Noncurrent, beyond one year", "Split by expected sale year", "Other long-term assets, by sale date"],
 "Current assets are those expected to be realized within one year or the operating cycle, whichever is longer. Inventory held through a long operating cycle stays current."),
("Which line appears on a multi-step income statement but not on a single-step one?",
 "Gross profit", ["Net income", "Income tax expense", "Total revenues"],
 "A multi-step statement shows intermediate subtotals such as gross profit and operating income. A single-step statement groups all revenues and all expenses and shows only net income."),
("Before closing the books, a company finds that a $12,000 payment for next year's insurance was recorded as insurance expense. Ignoring taxes, correcting it changes this year's net income by:",
 "An increase of $12,000", ["A decrease of $12,000", "No change in net income", "An increase of $6,000"],
 "The correction debits prepaid insurance and credits insurance expense for $12,000. Lower expense raises net income by $12,000."),
("A company sells an available-for-sale debt security on which it had recorded unrealized gains in accumulated OCI. On sale, those accumulated gains are:",
 "Reclassified into net income", ["Left in AOCI permanently", "Moved straight to retained earnings", "Reversed against the investment"],
 "A reclassification adjustment moves the realized amount out of AOCI and into net income, so the gain is not counted twice in comprehensive income."),
("Under the indirect method, amortization of a premium on the company's bonds payable is:",
 "Deducted from net income", ["Added to net income", "A financing inflow", "Not adjusted at all for cash flow"],
 "Premium amortization makes interest expense smaller than the cash interest paid. To get operating cash flow, the amortization is subtracted from net income."),
("A company using the indirect method must also disclose:",
 "Interest and income taxes paid", ["Dividends received and paid", "Depreciation by asset class", "Cash paid to suppliers"],
 "With the indirect method, cash paid for interest and for income taxes must be disclosed, either on the statement or in the notes. Cash paid to suppliers is a direct-method line."),
("Under the voting interest model, a company generally consolidates another entity when it owns:",
 "Over 50% of the voting shares", ["20% or more of the voting shares", "Any seat on the board", "Over 50% of its assets"],
 "A controlling financial interest, usually majority ownership of voting shares, requires consolidation. 20% to 50% usually signals significant influence and the equity method."),
("Which item appears in the statement of changes in equity but is not part of comprehensive income?",
 "Dividends declared", ["Net income", "Translation adjustments", "Unrealized gains on debt"],
 "Comprehensive income covers net income and OCI. Dividends are distributions to owners, so they change equity without being part of comprehensive income."),
("On January 1 a parent sells equipment with a carrying amount of $60,000 to its subsidiary for $75,000. The equipment has 5 years of remaining life, straight-line. On the consolidation worksheet at December 31, the unrealized gain still to be eliminated from the equipment is:",
 "$12,000", ["$15,000", "$3,000", "$0"],
 "The $15,000 intercompany gain is realized as the subsidiary depreciates the equipment, $15,000 / 5 = $3,000 a year. After one year $15,000 - $3,000 = $12,000 remains in the equipment's carrying amount and is eliminated."),
("An 80%-owned subsidiary declares dividends, part to its parent and part to its other shareholders. In consolidation, the dividends paid to the noncontrolling shareholders are reported as:",
 "A reduction of the noncontrolling interest", ["A cut to consolidated retained earnings", "Eliminated, with no effect at all", "An expense in consolidated net income"],
 "Dividends to the parent are intercompany and eliminated against its dividend income. Dividends to outside shareholders leave the group, so they reduce the noncontrolling interest in equity, not consolidated retained earnings."),
]
